{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1529640-for-those-with-knowledge-of-psychology","id":1529640,"title":"For those with knowledge of psychology","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-29T05:42:44-08:00","id":1529640,"title":"For those with knowledge of psychology","content":"<u><b><i>This post does not aim to cause controversy nor to make fun/light of mental conditions and illnesses. </i></b></u><br /> <br /> That being said, which known behaviours (positive or negative), characteristics, mental conditions (positive or negative) and/or mental illness could be associated with each Path, if any?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For example I was reading the Schizoid personality and their internal Fantasy world and JUST THAT PART sounded very Acanthus to me. And I remember from first edition how the Mastigos Path was prone to either sociopathy or psychopathy. But also the Moros being extremely Goal-Oriented.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course I could be wildly misinformed, and there is no association between those things and the Paths.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T08:47:51-08:00","id":1529646,"title":"","content":"Synaesthesia, body dysmorphic disorder and gender dysphoria, some of the spectrum of psychosexual disorders, and clinical zoanthropy I feel could have associations with Thyrsus - these might be the most easy and obvious answers to the question, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T09:22:36-08:00","id":1529648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Firebrand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1529640-for-those-with-knowledge-of-psychology?p=1529646#post1529646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Synaesthesia, body dysmorphic disorder and gender dysphoria, some of the spectrum of psychosexual disorders, and clinical zoanthropy I feel could have associations with Thyrsus - these might be the most easy and obvious answers to the question, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel Synaesthesia could also be Acanthus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}